as, Eastern Sawatch Mountains Above 11000 Feet, Central Lake\nCounty Below 11000 Feet and Western Chaffee County Between 9000 and\n11000 Feet.\n\n* WHEN...Until midnight MDT tonight.\n\n* IMPACTS...Heavy rainfall over the Willow burn scar will be possible\nup to and during the period of the watch. Residents near the Willow\nburn scar should prepare for potential debris flow. Be sure to stay\nup to date with information from local authorities. Heavy rainfall\ncould trigger flash flooding of low-lying areas, and debris flows\nin and near recent wildfire burn scars.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- National Weather Service Meteorologists are forecasting heavy\nrainfall over the burn scar, which may lead to flash flooding and\ndebris flows.\n- Some locations that may experience flash flooding include...\nLocations in and near the Willow Burn Scar, and the Chalk Cliffs.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-09-01T00:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Leadville Vicinity/Lake County Below 11000 Ft; Eastern Sawatch Mountains above 11000 Ft; Western Chaffee County Between 9000 and 11000 Ft","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.0a2d6fdad727609dde682d5c846133234061c16f.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.0a2d6fdad727609dde682d5c846133234061c16f.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"PUB","issued":"2026-08-31T23:41:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KPUB 312341 AFDPUB Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Pueblo CO 541 PM MDT Mon Aug 31 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - Shortwave will move across the region bring showers and thunderstorms to the area late this afternoon and evening; some of the activity will move across during the late evening/early AM hours. - Drier weather Tuesday through Thursday - Better monsoon flow pattern ","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=PUB&issuedby=PUB&product=AFD&format=CI"},"hwo":{"office":"PUB","issued":"2026-08-31T17:35:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FLUS45 KPUB 311735 HWOPUB Hazardous Weather Outlook